## 3. Owner entity and DTO classes

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — the telephone field carries JSR-380 validation annotations:
```java
@Column(name = "telephone")
@NotEmpty
@Digits(fraction = 0, integer = 10)
@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", message = "Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")
private String telephone;
```
(address and city are `@NotEmpty`.) Imports: `jakarta.validation.constraints.Digits`, `NotEmpty`, `Pattern`.

The DTO classes `OwnerFieldsDto` and `OwnerDto` do NOT exist as checked-in `.java` files. They are code-generated at build time from the OpenAPI spec `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`. The `telephone` constraints are declared in the `OwnerFields` schema (starts line 1991):
```yaml
    OwnerFields:
      title: Owner fields
      description: Editable fields of a pet owner.
      type: object
      properties:
        ...
        telephone:
          title: Telephone number
          description: The telephone number of the pet owner.
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 20
          pattern: '^[0-9]*$'
          example: '6085551023'
      required:
        - firstName
        - lastName
        - address
        - city
        - telephone
```
So the generated `OwnerFieldsDto.telephone` gets `@Size(min=1, max=20)`, `@Pattern(regexp="^[0-9]*$")`, and `@NotNull` (required). `OwnerDto` extends `OwnerFields` plus a read-only `id` and `pets` (schema `Owner`, line 2040).

## 4. All existing telephone validation

- OpenAPI `OwnerFields` schema (generated DTO): `minLength: 1`, `maxLength: 20`, `pattern: '^[0-9]*$'`, and `required`. This is the validation actually applied to the inbound POST body (the DTO). Note `^[0-9]*$` allows any length of digits (including empty since `*`), only bounded by min/maxLength.
- `Owner` entity (`Owner.java` lines 46-50): `@NotEmpty`, `@Digits(fraction=0, integer=10)`, `@Pattern(regexp="^[0-9]{10}$", message="Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")` — enforces exactly 10 digits. This is on the persistence entity.
- `RequireOwnerFields.java` (the create pipeline's validate step): only a null/blank presence check on telephone — no format/length/digit validation.
- DB schema: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/db/h2/schema.sql:37` → `telephone VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL`; `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/db/hsqldb/schema.sql:44` → `telephone VARCHAR(20)`. (mysql/postgres schemas also define telephone.)

There is NO normalization logic anywhere (no stripping of non-digit characters). The create pipeline validates presence only, then MapStruct copies telephone verbatim to the Owner entity.

## 5. Existing tests for creating owners / telephone

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — black-box tests hitting `POST /api/owners` then `GET /api/owners/{id}`:
```java
/** telephone-normalize: On create, normalize the telephone by removing every non-digit character, then require exa... */
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

    @Test
    void coreStripsToTenDigits() throws Exception {
        ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
        o.put("telephone", "(04) 1234-5678");
        int id = createOwnerOk(o);
        getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.telephone").value("0412345678"));
    }

    @Test
    void errorRejectsTooFewDigits() throws Exception {
        ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
        o.put("telephone", "12345");
        createOwner(o).andExpect(status().isBadRequest());
    }
}
```
These tests expect telephone normalization (strip non-digits) plus a "exactly 10 digits" rule — behavior that is NOT yet implemented in the create pipeline. `coreStripsToTenDigits` would currently fail at the DTO `pattern: '^[0-9]*$'` (parentheses/spaces/dash rejected) or would not normalize.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — the shared harness. Relevant helpers: `ownerNode()` (builds a valid unique owner with `telephone = uniqueTelephone()` → `"04%08d"`, a 10-digit AU mobile), `createOwner()` / `createOwnerOk()` (POST `/api/owners`), `getOwner(id)` (GET), `extractId()`. Runs under `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(roles={"OWNER_ADMIN",...})`.

Also present: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` (audit test support, not telephone-specific).

Nothing was modified.

